<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">V-E</span> </span><span id="S5.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">General Video Understanding</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike most existing image-to-video transfer learning methods which are tailored for one specific task, there have been some methods that aim to transfer the pretrained image-text knowledge across multiple tasks to achieve general video understanding. FitCLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite> proposes to train a student model by a small number of labeled video-text pairs and a large number of video-text pseudo labels, where the student model is then fused with the teacher model by weight ensembling for zero-shot video understanding. STAN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite> presents spatial-temporal auxiliary network as a side-tuning approach to perform temporal interaction and feature merging in the additional side branch, which achieves state-of-the-art performances across video-text retrieval and video action recognition.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<p id="S5.T3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T3.3.1" class="ltx_text"></span> 
<span id="S5.T3.3.2" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_block"><span id="S5.T3.3.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">TABLE III</span>: </span><span id="S5.T3.3.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Experimental results of representative methods with varied image-language foundation models and different image-to-video transfer learning strategies in coarse-grained video understanding tasks.</span></span>
<span id="S5.T3.3.2.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="S5.T3.3.2.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S5.T3.3.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt ltx_colspan ltx_colspan_9" style="padding-left:4.3pt;padding-right:4.3pt;"><span id="S5.T3.3.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Coarse-grained Video Understanding</span></span></span>
